  "problem": "Successful completion of nonobject Value pin could return true while confirmed metadata and exact tool-owner gate were absent; a newer task retired it and lazy TTL cleanup dropped confirmed tool ownership. Selected scalars/arrays also failed JavaScript object-spread semantics.",
  "changes": [
    "Normalize all JSON pin kinds at commit. Exact arena metadata retains UTF16 code-unit string properties, including generated lone surrogates; Value observation repairs only those units without truncating existing opaque members.",
    "Expose immutable get_metadata_exact with the same lazy expiry and ambiguity policy as get_exact.",
    "Keep a private confirmation flag on the owned Pin; both tool-owner lookup and Router continuity labeling read it. Selection resets it; only validated current completion sets it.",
    "Separate raw Value selection retention (original toolModels.length truthiness) from exact native selection retention (typed tools). Completion replaces retention with validated exact evidence.",
    "Retain exact-origin on staged attempts so completion restores requestedModel units for exact inputs while preserving arbitrary Value requestedModel metadata/absence."
  ],
  "api_boundaries": [
    "Construct native Pin with Pin::new rather than a struct literal; the new private confirmation field prevents caller mutation from forging confirmation. Public exact identities/tools remain editable before ownership transfer.",
    "get and Pin.value are explicitly lossy metadata observations for generated surrogate units. get_metadata_exact is the exact document; model/tool/request identities remain JsString, never reconstructed from repaired observations.",
    "Value adapter supports JSON metadata, not JavaScript getters/prototypes/mutable object aliases. Typed tool evidence is not arbitrary JavaScript extension-object identity. No whole-API or whole-area parity approval is inferred."
  ],
